# <%= projectName || 'Laravel App' %>

A Laravel backend application generated by BotKelp.

## Project Setup

### Prerequisites

- PHP 8.2+
- Composer (PHP dependency manager)
- MySQL 8.0+ or PostgreSQL 15+
- Node.js 18+ (optional, for frontend assets)

### Install Dependencies

```bash
# Install PHP dependencies
composer install

# Install Node.js dependencies (if using frontend assets)
npm install

# Copy environment file
cp .env.example .env

# Generate application key
php artisan key:generate
```

## Environment Configuration

```bash
# Edit .env with your configuration
nano .env
```

### Environment Variables

| Variable | Description | Default |
|----------|-------------|---------|
| `APP_NAME` | Application name | Laravel |
| `APP_ENV` | Application environment | local |
| `APP_KEY` | Encryption key (generate with `php artisan key:generate`) | - |
| `APP_DEBUG` | Debug mode (true/false) | true |
| `APP_URL` | Application URL | http://localhost |
| `DB_CONNECTION` | Database driver | mysql |
| `DB_HOST` | Database host | 127.0.0.1 |
| `DB_PORT` | Database port | 3306 |
| `DB_DATABASE` | Database name | laravel |
| `DB_USERNAME` | Database username | root |
| `DB_PASSWORD` | Database password | - |

## Running the Development Server

### Using PHP Built-in Server

```bash
# Start the development server
php artisan serve
```

Starts the development server at `http://localhost:8000`

### Using Laravel Sail (Docker)

```bash
# Build and start containers
./vendor/bin/sail up -d

# Run migrations
./vendor/bin/sail artisan migrate

# View logs
./vendor/bin/sail logs -f
```

## Running with Docker Compose

```bash
# Build and start all services
docker-compose up -d --build

# Run migrations
docker-compose exec app php artisan migrate

# Generate application key
docker-compose exec app php artisan key:generate

# View logs
docker-compose logs -f

# Stop all services
docker-compose down
```

