## API Endpoints

The following API endpoints are available:

### Health
- `GET /api/health` - Health check

### Examples
- `GET /api/examples` - List all examples (with pagination)
- `POST /api/examples` - Create a new example
- `GET /api/examples/{id}` - Get a specific example
- `PUT /api/examples/{id}` - Update an example
- `DELETE /api/examples/{id}` - Delete an example
- `PATCH /api/examples/{id}/toggle-active` - Toggle example active status

## Adding Endpoints

1. Create a new controller or add a method to an existing controller
2. Add the route in `routes/api.php`

Example:

```php
// In app/Http/Controllers/ExampleController.php
public function newMethod(Request $request): JsonResponse
{
    return response()->json(['message' => 'Hello from new method']);
}

// In routes/api.php
Route::get('/new-endpoint', [ExampleController::class, 'newMethod']);
```

## Adding Models

1. Create a new model with migration

```bash
php artisan make:model NewModel -m
```

2. Define the model and migration

```php
// In app/Models/NewModel.php
namespace App\Models;

use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Model;

class NewModel extends Model
{
    protected $fillable = ['name', 'value'];
}

// In database/migrations/xxxx_xx_xx_xxxxxx_create_new_models_table.php
public function up(): void
{
    Schema::create('new_models', function (Blueprint $table) {
        $table->id();
        $table->string('name');
        $table->integer('value');
        $table->timestamps();
    });
}
```

