## Authentication

Laravel includes built-in authentication. To set it up:

```bash
# Install Laravel Breeze (recommended)
composer require laravel/breeze --dev
php artisan breeze:install
npm install && npm run dev
php artisan migrate
```

Or use Laravel Sanctum for API authentication:

```bash
composer require laravel/sanctum
php artisan vendor:publish --provider="Laravel\Sanctum\SanctumServiceProvider"
php artisan migrate
```

## Deployment Options

### Laravel Forge

1. Create a new server on Forge
2. Connect your GitHub repository
3. Deploy with Forge

### Railway

```bash
# Install Railway CLI
npm install -g @railway/cli

# Deploy
railway init
railway add mysql
railway add redis
railway up
```

### Render

1. Create a new Web Service on Render
2. Connect your GitHub repository
3. Set the build command: `composer install --no-dev --optimize-autoloader`
4. Set the start command: `php artisan serve --host=0.0.0.0 --port=$PORT`

### AWS Elastic Beanstalk

```bash
# Install EB CLI
pip install awsebcli

# Initialize EB
eb init -p php-8.2 laravel-app --region us-west-2

# Create environment and deploy
eb create laravel-env
```

### Google Cloud Run

```bash
# Build and push to Google Container Registry
gcloud builds submit --tag gcr.io/YOUR_PROJECT_ID/laravel-app

# Deploy to Cloud Run
gcloud run deploy laravel-app \
  --image gcr.io/YOUR_PROJECT_ID/laravel-app \
  --platform managed \
  --region us-central1 \
  --allow-unauthenticated \
  --port 8000
```

